  "title": "Avocado boats with balsamic vinegar",
  "description": "Eat avocado halves with tea spoon.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<p>You are missing out if you haven't made this incredible snack from ripe avocados. Anybody can make it, even my 7 year old makes it when she comes home from school. This is her favorite way to eat avocado. Split it in half and fill the center stone hole with some balsamic vinegar. Enjoy this healthy, delicious snack or appetizer. </p>\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21607,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1625719471344} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21607-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Avocado boats with balsamic vinegar</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/IMG_8363.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tEat avocado halves with tea spoon.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>3 avocados</li><li>salt and freshly ground pepper (optional)</li><li>6 tsp balsamic vinegar</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Cut the avocados in half lengthwise, remove pits but do not peel them. Season with salt and freshly ground pepper. Add 1 tsp of balsamic vinegar in each hole, and serve. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/IMG_7547.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizers</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
